{"text": "ekerSeamans Chern & Mellot, LLC TEL \u2014_808:788.7740\night and Main FAX 8046982950\nNS 707 East Main Stest sw eckerscamans.com\nSuit 1450,\n\nATTORNEYS AT LAW Richmond, VA23219\nAnthony F Toy\n(808) 18-795 ites)\ntuoydecerscamanscom\nJuly 18, 2013\nVIA FIRST CLASS MAIL\nJ. Jasen Eige\n\nCounselor and Senior Policy Advisor\nOffice of the Governor of Virginia\nPatrick Henry Building, 3rd Floor\n1111 East Broad Street\nRichmond, Virginia 23219\n\nDear Mr. Eige:\n\nOn April 26, 2013, I was appointed by the Attorney General as Special Counsel to the\nGovemor of Virginia and the Office of the Governor. As you know, I served as Attorney\nGeneral from 1977-1978. Since that time, I have worked in private practice as an attorney in\nRichmond and served on the executive committees of two national law firms. I am a member of\nthe Society of Attomeys General Emeritus. 1 previously served on a special panel on ethical\nissues in complex litigation, reporting to the National Commission for Review of Antitrust Laws\nand Procedure. I am a Fellow and former board member of the Virginia Law Foundation; a\nFellow of the American Bar Foundation; a past member of the Couneil for the Future of the\nNational Judicial College; a past faculty member of the Virginia State Bar (Professionalism\nCommittee, 1994-1997; Past Chair, Special Committee on Resolution of Fee Disputes); and a\nmember of the Boyd Graves Conference. I have also held teaching positions, a Chair at the\nUniversity of Richmond School of Law, and have lectured at the School of Business of the\nCollege of William & Mary,\n\nLast month, I was asked to conduct an audit to determine whether any gubernatorial\nappointments were made to either Jonnie Williams or to any other officer of Star Scientific, Inc.,\nor Rock Creek Pharmaceuticals, Inc., during the McDonnell administration, or whether any\nCommonwealth funds, grants, or contracts were awarded to these entities or persons. I also\nincluded within the scope of my review a determination whether any public funds, grants,\ncontracts, or appointments were made to the Roskamp Institute or any officer of Roskamp. For\nconvenience in reading this report, I refer to these entities and persons \u2014Star Scientific, Rock\nCreek, Roskamp, and their officers, including Jonnie Williams \u2014 collectively as \u201cStar\nScientific.\u201d I have concluded my audit and submit this report.\n\nBased on my review, there have been no public funds, grants, or contracts from the\nagencies discussed below to Star Scientific. Likewise, there have been no gubematorial\nappointments made to Jonnie Williams or any officer of Star Scientific.",
